  "paragraphs": [
    "Jins ‘Ajam has two versions:",
    "The 5-note version of Jins ‘Ajam is the most common version, and is the first jins in Maqam ‘Ajam and Maqam Shawq Afza. It is notated here with its tonic on C and its ghammaz on G.",
    "Click the notes and hold using the mouse to hear them play.",
    "The 3-note version of Jins ‘Ajam occurs mostly when it is used as a secondary jins, for example on the 6th scale degree of Maqam Bayati, Maqam Saba or Maqam Kurd. This version is a carry over from Maqam ‘Ajam ‘Ushayran. It is notated here with its tonic on B♭.",
    "Click the notes and hold using the mouse to hear them play."
  ],
  "text": "Jins ‘Ajam Root jins of the Maqam ‘Ajam Family Jins Index Pronunciation of ‘Ajam Jins ‘Ajam has two versions: The 5-note version of Jins ‘Ajam is the most common version, and is the first jins in Maqam ‘Ajam and Maqam Shawq Afza . It is notated here with its tonic on C and its ghammaz on G. Click the notes and hold using the mouse to hear them play. The 3-note version of Jins ‘Ajam occurs mostly when it is used as a secondary jins , for example on the 6 th scale degree of Maqam Bayati , Maqam Saba or Maqam Kurd . This version is a carry over from Maqam ‘Ajam ‘Ushayran . It is notated here with its tonic on B♭. Click the notes and hold using the mouse to hear them play. Jins ‘Ajam 5-note version examples Aghadan Alqaka (1971) Umm Kulthum Music by Muhammad Abdel Wahab (Egypt) el-Buwab (1994) Fairouz Music by Philemon Wehbe Fi Youm we Leila (1978) Warda Music by Muhammad Abdel Wahab (Egypt) Lissa Fakir (1960) Umm Kulthum Music by Riyad al-Sunbati Mawwal Min Youm Furgak Muhammad Khayri Til‘it Ya Mahla Nurha Muhammad Abdel Karim Music by Sayed Darwish Jins ‘Ajam 3-note version examples Ba‘id ‘Annak (1965) Umm Kulthum Music by Baligh Hamdi (Egypt) 3-note Jins ‘Ajam on the 6 th degree of Maqam Bayati Habba Fouq w Habba Taht Ahmad Adaweya Music by Mohamed el-Mesery 3-note Jins ‘Ajam on the 6 th degree of Maqam Saba Ahu Da-lli Sar Nay Barghouthi Music by Sayed Darwish 3-note Jins ‘Ajam on the 6 th degree of Maqam Kurd",
